===[[Poké Problem]]===
[[File:Poké Problem quiz data broadcast.jpg|thumb|Buttons to choose an answer at the bottom and the prize at the right of the screen.]]
Viewers could answer the Poké Problem with their remotes during the airing of SM003 and SM004, which aired as a one-hour special, to take part in a lottery of five {{DL|Pokémon Z-Ring|Z-Ring and Z-Crystal Special Set|Pokémon Z-Ring and Z-Crystal Special Sets}}. During the airing of SM009 viewers could take part in a lottery of ten [http://archives.bulbagarden.net/wiki/File:MonColl%C3%A9_GET_Monster_Balls_Filled_With_Voices_and_MonColl%C3%A9_GET_Pikachu_figures.png MonCollé GET Monster Balls Filled With Voices and MonCollé GET Pikachu figures].

3 points are given to viewers who get the answer right, and 1 point to viewers who get the answer wrong. If the viewer collects 10 points during one lottery period a password will appear which can be used as an entry for the lottery. Viewers can then reset the score and start collecting again for another entry for the lottery.

===Plot overview and introduction of the characters===
[[File:Data broadcast SM cropped.jpg|thumb|Button for an introduction of the main characters and a short overview of the series plot.]]
Viewers can see an introduction of the main characters and a short overview of the series plot using their remote.
